#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Flatline agent: know before your server flatlines.

usage:
  flatline status [--json]   vitals and current problems (the Mac app runs this over SSH)
  flatline watch             check forever and alert on Telegram (run by systemd)
  flatline setup             connect a Telegram bot interactively
  flatline telegram          read a bot token and chat id from stdin (used by the Mac app)
  flatline share             make a one-time, 24-hour invite for read-only access (used by the Mac app)
  flatline access [--json]   list who has read-only access; flatline revoke NAME takes it away
  flatline uninstall         remove Flatline and everything it created
  flatline --version

Without installing anything, `python3 - status --json --live < flatline` reads a server once and leaves no trace.

It only reads: no listening ports, no remote commands, no shell, Python standard library only.
"""
